{
 "title": "ISO Status M transmission densitometry \u2014 spectral responsivities",
 "source": "ISO 5-3 / ANSI CGATS.5-1993 Status M, values as embedded in ArgyllCMS xspect.c (denM), cross-validated: same file's Status A table matches this project's StatusA_ISO5-3.json exactly",
 "notes": [
  "Status M densitometry is the reference response for measuring colour-negative films (unmasked to the print process); used here for Kodak Portra 400 which publishes Status M characteristic curves.",
  "log10_spectral_products_as_published are the log10 spectral products normalized to a 5.000 peak per channel, exactly as tabulated in the ArgyllCMS denM table (Status M).",
  "Deeply negative log-product values (roughly v < -3) are linear-slope extrapolations of the published response beyond the meaningfully tabulated band; they sit far below the 1e-3-of-peak floor and contribute nothing to integration.",
  "responsivity_linear_peak1 = 10^(v-5); any point with v < -3 (i.e. below 1e-3 of the 5.000 peak in log space, hence < 1e-8 linear after the peak-1 renormalization) is floored to 0.0.",
  "Grid 400-770 nm at 10 nm. Status M red support extends to 770 nm; consumers whose dye data ends at 700 nm truncate and renormalize the red responsivity (documented at point of use)."
 ],
